{:id "0003-worker-core"
 :title "Worker core: decide when and how the agent replies"
 :lupa/area :agent
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "The pure decisions behind the agent's turn: whether a conversation
        is waiting on the agent, what to send an engine, how to read what the
        engine says back (tolerantly), and the reply message to write. The
        I/O worker built later only fetches, calls, and stores."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/worker/core.clj" "test/halfahead/worker/core_test.clj"]
 :design "New namespace halfahead.worker.core (.clj: the worker runs only in
          Babashka; cheshire.core is available there for JSON). Public fns:

          (awaiting-reply agent-id messages) -> message or nil
            messages are :ha/message maps of one conversation, any order.
            Returns the latest message by :sent-at when its author is not
            the agent and no agent message was sent after it; else nil.
            (Derived, never stored.)

          (engine-request persona members messages) -> :ha/engine-request
            history = the conversation's messages sorted by :sent-at, the
            last 200 at most, each as {:role :human|:agent :text}, where the
            role is the author member's :kind (an author not in members
            counts as :human).

          (engine-prompt request) -> string
            The persona, then a short instruction block, then the transcript.
            The instructions tell the engine to answer with ONE JSON object
            {\"text\": ..., \"delivery\": ..., \"emphasis\": [...]} and nothing
            else; list the five deliveries with one line each on when to use
            them (plain: the default; typed: when the pause itself means
            something; headline: one striking point, with 1-3 emphasis
            phrases copied exactly from the text; aside: a quiet remark or
            caveat; credits: thanks, attributions, or a short list). Say:
            prefer plain; flair must serve the meaning. The transcript labels
            turns 'Human:' and 'You:'.

          (parse-reply s) -> :ha/engine-reply
            Tolerant reader. If s contains a JSON object (possibly inside
            ```json fences or surrounded by prose), read it; unknown delivery
            -> :plain; missing or non-string emphasis items dropped, at most
            8; text over 4000 characters truncated at 4000. If no usable JSON
            object with a non-blank text is found, the whole trimmed s is the
            text with :plain delivery and no emphasis. Blank s throws
            ex-info {:type :ha/empty-reply}.

          (resolve-emphasis text phrases) -> [[from to] ...]
            First occurrence of each phrase in text; phrases not found are
            dropped; a span overlapping an earlier kept span is dropped;
            sorted by from; at most 8.

          (reply-message {:reply r :to message :agent-id a :id id :now inst})
            -> :ha/message with the reply's text and delivery, emphasis
            resolved from its phrases, :in-reply-to the replied message's
            :id, the same :conversation-id, :sent-at now. The result must be
            a valid :ha/message (assert in tests via halfahead.schema)."
 :examples
 ["parse-reply of \"Sure!\\n```json\\n{\\\"text\\\": \\\"Hi there\\\", \\\"delivery\\\": \\\"aside\\\", \\\"emphasis\\\": []}\\n```\" -> {:text \"Hi there\" :delivery :aside :emphasis []}"
  "parse-reply of \"just words\" -> {:text \"just words\" :delivery :plain :emphasis []}"
  "resolve-emphasis \"the cat sat on the mat\" [\"cat\" \"dog\" \"the mat\"] -> [[4 7] [15 22]]"]
 :acceptance
 ["awaiting-reply: returns the human's latest message when the agent has not
   answered after it; nil when the agent's message is the latest; nil for no
   messages; order of input does not matter"
  "engine-request: valid :ha/engine-request; roles follow member kinds; at
   most 200 turns, the most recent ones, in time order"
  "engine-prompt contains the persona, all five delivery names, the JSON
   shape, and the transcript with 'Human:' and 'You:' labels in order"
  "parse-reply handles every example above, a bare JSON object, a JSON
   object with an unknown delivery (-> :plain), over-long text (-> 4000
   chars), and throws :ha/empty-reply on blank input; every non-throwing
   result is a valid :ha/engine-reply"
  "resolve-emphasis matches the example, never returns overlapping spans,
   and every span is within the text"
  "reply-message returns a valid :ha/message with :in-reply-to set"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit halfahead.schema, bb.edn, or the test runner"
  "No network, no Firestore, no shelling out to an engine, no clock reads,
   no persona text (the persona is an input)"]
 :context ["DESIGN.md" "docs/SCHEMA.md" "src/halfahead/schema.cljc"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
